4. **What stays open, said in the README `## Limits`, each with a cell that proves the bound that DOES hold:** after a time-out, a refresher that ignores cancellation can still be running when the next refresh starts (D21); a wall clock set back while the server runs, then a restart inside the window, lengthens a session's idle life by at most the step (D24); a blocking event handler blocks the callers of that refresh (D28, text only).
