## Questions with defaults (Tuesday answers at the stamp; every default is already assumed above)
- **Q21 (the moved `main`; STOP-CLASS: S4 must answer it in words).** Default: never rebase the pushed `70c1fad5`; if `main` moved and touches none of the lane's paths or the solution file, push the one new commit fast-forward and name the moved `main`; if it touches one, STOP. Alternative A (the commission's words read literally): rebase both commits onto the new `main` and push with `--force-with-lease`; needs Tuesday to lift the force-push hold IN WORDS, and both readers then re-read the whole lane as rebased, not a delta. Alternative B: merge `origin/main` into the branch (a second new commit, a merge commit; the squash at landing flattens it). Cost of the default: the head's hosted run does not include `main`'s newer commits (the pull request's `pull_request` run does, at landing); cost of A: a rewritten reviewed commit; cost of B: two commits, one of them a merge for the readers to read.
- Q22 (D20). Default: `Task.Run` around the refresher call, locals captured first. Alternative: `await Task.Yield()` at the top of `RefreshAsync` (B1838's other suggestion) with `RefreshAsync` itself started without awaiting. Cost of the default: a pool hop per refresh; cost of the alternative: `Task.Yield` continues on the caller's context when one exists (UNMEASURED for the host), so the bound may not start at once under a synchronisation context.
- Q23 (D21). Default: a README limit line and F13 proving the bound that holds. Alternative: close it (no new call while the timed-out one runs). Costs in D21.
- Q24 (D22). Default: F15 by a `NewToken` handler that signs out; U03 over the faulty kit with a `Saves` count and no `NewToken`. Alternative: F15 by a held refresher and a sign-out raced on two threads (as B1839's S03). Cost of the alternative: a race the cell cannot make deterministic.
- Q25 (D23). Default: re-check in `ObtainAsync` after the await, both clocks, `Expired`. Alternative: also refuse to ACCEPT an answer once idle has passed (check inside `AcceptLocked`). Cost of the alternative: one more rule and its cell; the default already hands nothing out and erases the record.
- Q26 (D24). Default: README limit line plus E08 (the bound). Alternative: re-anchor at every write and at `Sweep` on drift. Costs in D24.
- Q27 (D25). Default: a clearing array-backed writer, no pool, cell P04 by its cleared report. Alternative A: pre-size at 6 bytes per character, proved by allocation; Alternative B: bound user and subject length. Costs in D25.
- Q28 (D26). Default: R08 (crafted `written`), R09 (failing read: erased, as built), each with its mutant. Alternative for R09's behaviour: a failing read at restart throws `StoreFailed` from the constructor (as a failing listing does since ANSWER-1) and erases nothing. Cost of the alternative: a behaviour change this round was not asked for; cost of the default: a transient read error at start erases the sessions it hits (fail closed; README line).
- Q29 (D27). Default: (a) text "less than", R10 pins the edge; (b) `SignOutReason.RestartWindow` removed, the README names four reasons, V02. Alternative for (b): keep it as reserved, documented as raised by no path. Cost of the default: a public enum member leaves an unreleased library (0 uses outside the enum, MEASURED); cost of the alternative: a value no handler can ever receive.
- Q30 (D28). Default: B07; the blocking-handler line in README `## Limits` and FOR RECORDS. Alternative: the handler line in FOR RECORDS only (Tuesday's words "stays a records line (no code)" read narrowly). Cost: none in code either way.
- Q31 (how "red first" reads). Default: a code change's cell red against the round-1 code; a guarded-rule cell red against the round-1 code with its mutant applied (THE CONTROLS). Alternative: only code-change cells need a red-first; guarded-rule cells are proved by the Step-4 mutants on the fixed code alone. Cost of the default: eight more heavy jobs in Step 3.
- Q32 (names). Default: the cell names of THE CONTROLS, `ClearingBufferWriter`, the cells in the existing test files.
- Q33 (mutant runs). Default: this round's twelve plus round 1's mTimeout, mRace, mLate on the fixed code, each run over the lane's test project (a project path, its total printed), the whole suite before and after. Alternative: the whole suite per mutant. Cost of the default: a mutant's effect outside the lane's project is not seen (none is possible: nothing else references the library, MEASURED by the release guard counts); cost of the alternative: fifteen whole-suite runs on a shared lock.
- Q34 (windows and pane). Default: READY at Step 0 + 180 minutes, the push by Step 0 + 140, pane `Datasec/OXPd2-X18` (a new pane), level opus, the wave's heavy lock as in round 1 (Tuesday's ruling 8).
- Q35 (the gate). Default: G1 round 2 of 2, a DELTA review by BOTH readers, each re-running what FOR TUESDAY names.

